        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "007829e8-2b65-50c5-846a-5f1e6542ef9b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dean Jones, Laurens van der Post\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions\n- Works: The Million Dollar Duck, The $1,000,000 Duck, A Far Off Place, A Far-Off Place, A Story Like the Wind, The Love Bug, Beethoven\n- Topics: American comedy films, adventure drama films, film adaptations, Golden Globe nominations\n\nFacts:\n- Walt Disney Productions produced The Million Dollar Duck, a 1971 American comedy film also titled The $1,000,000 Duck, about a goose that lays golden eggs.\n- Dean Jones played Albert Dooley in The Million Dollar Duck in 1971 and received a Golden Globe nomination for that role.\n- Laurens van der Post wrote A Story Like the Wind in 1972.\n- Laurens van der Post wrote A Far-Off Place in 1974.\n- A Far Off Place is a 1993 American adventure drama film based on Laurens van der Post's works A Far-Off Place and A Story Like the Wind.\n- Dean Jones played Jim Douglas in The Love Bug in 1968 and Dr. Herman Varnick in Beethoven in 1992.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
